In a recent survey, it was found that the probability that a randomly selected person is in the group of `$ctx[A]` is `$pA_disp`, and the probability that they are in the group of `$ctx[B]` is `$pB_disp`. The probability that they are in the group of `$ctx[overlap]` is `$pAnd_disp`.

